! line DRAFT for user review — NOT yet submitted. Archival space-based precovery astrometry of
! line (88268) = 2001 KK76 (TNO), measured from four public HST ACS/HRC CLEAR exposures (GO
! line program 10514; rootnames J9FW91HPQ/HQQ/HRQ/HSQ), 2006-05-02, retrieved from MAST.
! line Object positions were solved against the Gaia-DR3-registered Hubble Source Catalog v3.0
! line (HSC30) astrometric reference frame; astCat therefore reported as Gaia3 (HSC30 is the
! line intermediary — see remarks). Per-axis uncertainties are set to rmsRA=0.16" / rmsDec=0.10"
! line by referee mandate (conservative floor; the internal centroiding formal errors are a few
! line tens of mas and are NOT used). The HST obscode is 250; because 250 is a spacecraft with no
! line geocentric coordinates, each row carries the geocentric equatorial-J2000 (ICRF) position of
! line HST (sys=ICRF_KM, ctr=399, pos1/2/3 in km) taken from the JPL Horizons HST ephemeris
! line (body -48) at each mid-exposure UTC; find_orb applies this satellite parallax (verified:
! line dropping the offsets makes 250 unusable, confirming the parallax is genuinely in the fit).
! line obsTime is UTC (the CSV column jd_tdb_mid actually held UTC JD; treated as UTC throughout;
! line TT-UTC = 65.184 s in 2006 is handled internally by the orbit code, ~0.05" along-track).
! line PHOTOMETRY: exposures are unfiltered CLEAR(HRC); the source magnitudes are non-standard
! line lower bounds only, so NO calibrated photometry is reported (mag/band deliberately omitted).
! line ACTION BEFORE SUBMISSION: contact the MPC SARC (Singletons and Archival observations
! line Committee, minorplanetcenter.net/mpcops/documentation/sarc/) for first-time archival-
! line submitter verification and file review; confirm the space-based (obscode 250) block and
! line satellite-offset conventions and the HSC30/Gaia3 astCat choice with the SARC member.
